      "body": "\n### \ud83d\udca1 Codex Review\n\nhttps://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/blob/1216fe4ffe3b78d5579c77d6b5090320c9a30e1d/tdf-hq/src/TDF/ServerAuth.hs#L1721-L1724\n**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Require an explicit new-account signal before creating**\n\nWhen a legacy Google user signs in through an older mobile build or a cached pre-change web bundle, the subject has no binding, and that client handles the consent error by retrying with the accepted terms version. This branch interprets that existing payload as authorization to create a new Party, so the user lands in a duplicate empty account while their roles and data remain attached to the legacy credential. Require a creation-intent field that legacy clients cannot send, or otherwise distinguish this case before inserting the Party.\n    \n\n<details> <summary>\u2139\ufe0f About Codex in GitHub</summary>\n<br/>\n\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\n- Open a pull request for review\n- Mark a draft as ready\n- Comment \"@codex review\".\n\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with \ud83d\udc4d.\n\n\n\n\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR. Try commenting \"@codex address that feedback\".\n            \n</details>",
